From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 18:21:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] docs(deploy): document what a Databricks App needs after the
 first deploy

deploy/databricks/README.md gets an app running, but what a working
deployment needs next was undocumented or only discoverable from code
(https://github.com/Desidero/omnigent/issues/17). Add a "Configuring the
app" section, written against the code at this base:

- how the server config reaches an app, how to tell that it loaded, and
  which config keys the Apps entry point honours (admins and
  allowed_domains are not passed through);
- smart routing: why it is off on an app, the `routing:` block that
  turns it on, who calls the router and what is sent;
- the MCP registry, the per-user Databricks connection and its
  credential store, sharing defaults, that sessions need a host, the
  OTel schema, and deploy practicalities;
- every `sandbox.databricks` key, and `sandbox.host_config`.

Settings are shown through the deployment overlay and the KMS service
credential option, which is why this series needs both of those series.
Statements that come from one deployment's experience and cannot be
checked in this repository (managed MCP URL shapes, the read-only
catalog failure, the --compute-size resize) are marked as not verified;
the others the issue marked unverified are left out.

Not upstream yet: not proposed, and there is no contribution branch for
it. Most of it would apply upstream without the overlay examples.

